    "publishedAt": "2026-11-21",
    "summary": "This puts the plans of the government-backed startup to begin mass production of chips in 2027 at risk. Rapidus began to produce test structures with 2nm-class Gate-All-Around (GAA) transistors at its IIM-1 facility in Hokkaido in July 2025, nearly 16 months ago. Previously, Rapidus had specified its production targets without specifying calendar years or fiscal years, which by default implied the calendar year. Before it can mass-produce processors for customers, the company must demonstrate functional SRAM cells, integrate them into larger arrays, achieve acceptable yields, qualify its process technology, and then initiate risk production around a year before the start of high-volume manufacturing (HVM).",
