    "publishedAt": "2026-11-17",
    "summary": "This rule significantly addresses a long-standing gap in U.S. export controls, where Chinese companies that are barred from accessing NVIDIA's latest GPUs have been renting overseas computing power instead of purchasing the chips outright. Under the new rule, a license is required to ship any advanced accelerators to any data center worldwide that provides more than 12 million \"aggregate TPP\" of computing power to companies headquartered in Macau or Country Group D:5, which includes China. TPP, or Total Processing Performance, is BIS's metric for chip computing power, calculated as a chip's peak dense throughput multiplied by the bit length of the operation. Data centers already serving such customers have 90 days to obtain a license.",
